- Account deletion: Atomically remove current/historical username privilege
  references without erasing comments/files/history or other members. Keep
  display-only author provenance through copies/exchange/moves, prune it on
  deletion, stop orphan timers and guard the last board admin. Verify real
  browser confirmation/recreation
  and independent SQLite rollback snapshots.
- Expired native sessions: Reject messages before dispatch and return a login
  reload without the native alert/backtrace path; verify stale writes and browser
  navigation after account deletion.
- Native session lifecycle: Persist nonreused account versions, revoke stale
  browsers after password changes/resets/recreation, keep the changing browser
  signed in and require old unversioned sessions to sign in again. Transact
  credentials/versions/token revocation and serialize login with mutations;
  verify source/archive sessions, legacy negatives and reset-commit rollback.
- Database transactions: Recover shared connections after failed driver
  Begin/Commit/Rollback commands; discard pending writes despite Gambas nesting
  counter drift. Force real SQLite commit failures for accounts/cards, verify
  atomic history/content and later writes, and exercise first-admin races.
- Native membership UI: Add member/role/remove controls, role-aware menus and
  editors, Worker self-assignment/movement, translated captions, anchored refresh
  and disabled HTML/ARIA states; test two sessions, forged writes and mobile UI.
- Assigned/Worker roles: Scope every card read and relationship/history/export
  path, support multiple assignees and restrict Workers to moves/self-assignment/
  comments. Retain assignments in copies/imports/moves and test hidden WIP counts.
- Shared board permissions: Add member/admin/write/comment/read-only checks
  throughout native stores, transactional membership changes and personal stars/
  watch preferences; verify negative operations and current WeKan capabilities.
- Static asset boundary: Reject encoded/dot traversal, library/icon escapes,
  backslashes and control bytes before CGI; verify public/private test canaries.
- CGI deadlines: Capture private file-backed output so inherited descendant
  handles cannot keep timeout cleanup blocked; verify a real child process.
- Documentation: Describe runtime origin/POST boundaries, proxy configuration,
  initial REST contracts, token lifecycle/throttling and remaining test parity.
- Native large-text updates: Bypass environment/dispatcher limits using a
  short event and a private request file. Limit updates to current-form text
  controls; verify Unicode persistence, rejected events and cleanup on failure.
- Build: Discover shared Gambas tools from the new .tools/w/weba layout; test
  standalone/legacy/nested layouts, spaces and explicit tool overrides.
- REST authentication: Add login/logout, expiring hashed Bearer tokens, scoped
  board reads, all/presented-token revocation and password-reset invalidation.
  Separate API/browser identity, throttle peer login attempts, honor WITH_API
  and verify source/archive HTTP authentication and authorization boundaries.
- Native transport security: Move commands to POST bodies, validate request
  origin/authority and require a custom header for mutations/uploads/callbacks.
  Deny framing, add referrer/nosniff headers and test browser/CGI integration.
- Security: Block development/environment-dump routes, including encoded paths,
  before invoking Gambas; verify host and real packaged HTTP boundaries.
- Security: Remove login request/query/user-agent logging and the unused shared
  temporary logfile sink; guard against credential-bearing payload logging.

* Sat Nov 07 2026 Lauri Ojansivu <x@xet7.org> 1.0.0 (unreleased)
- Documentation: Describe preset/color-wheel use and refresh, verification
  coverage and pending full board gradient/special-theme styling.
- Colors: Add native preset swatches from WeKan and a custom browser color
  wheel, synchronized with the hex field. Keep context palettes, validation
  and persisted values; verify packaged Chromium and mobile positioning.
  Board theme choices use solid color samples; import the custom-color label.
- Documentation: Update native-menu/card/exchange instructions and TODO with
  verified coverage, format/file limits and remaining feature parity.
- Card detail editor: Refresh visible controls when tree selection changes the
  entry kind; verify checklist selection in the packaged browser workflow.
- Registration: Release result cursors before transactional writes/rollback and
  hash before taking the transaction; retain atomic first-Admin claiming. Verify
  three consecutive store/concurrent-signup runs after reproducing contention.
- Translations: Import 91 matching keys for 237 languages, covering new native
  menus and card controls while preserving user-provided popup titles.
- JSON exchange: Export/import weba-2 boards and scoped containers with empty
  layouts, ordering, archive state, rich content and attachments. Remap IDs in
  a transaction into a new board; validate malformed input and native file UI.
- Workspace actions: Add transactional cross-board moves preserving rich card
  data and relationships; delete archived items with title confirmation, owner
  checks and dependent-record cleanup. Test SQLite and packaged browser flows.
- Native menus: Add persisted board/list/swimlane/card actions, scoped history,
  archive restoration, WIP enforcement and JSON card export. Add comments,
  checklists, real subtasks, dependencies, typed fields, timers and binary
  attachments; validate ownership and rich-copy relationships with SQLite
  and real Chromium menu, upload and download tests.
- Lists: Persist stable card/list identities, retain legacy assignments and
  allow duplicate titles without merging cards during display or movement.

* Fri Nov 06 2026 Lauri Ojansivu <x@xet7.org> 1.0.0 (unreleased)
- Touch drag/drop: Add card/list/swimlane handles, ordering, cross-list/lane
  movement, edge auto-scroll, cancellation and mouse/keyboard input. Persist
  validated moves transactionally and retain native touch scrolling; add store,
  gesture, HTTP and real Chromium touch-event regression tests.
- Popups: Place card details beside the initiating action, clamp windows to the
  visual viewport and add top-right close controls with Escape support; verify
  portrait/landscape positioning, scrolling, menu/composer dismissal and native
  keyboard focus alignment/restoration.
- Icons: Use WeKan’s Font Awesome assets and compatibility aliases throughout
  native navigation, tree items, reports and board controls.
- Boards: Default to Swimlanes; align header/footer controls with WeKan, persist
  empty swimlanes/custom lists, place new lists after the selected one and route
  card actions to the native editor. Add store, DOM, HTTP and browser regressions.
- Translations: Import matching WeKan texts for 237 languages, add persistent
  login/account language selection, RTL and localized report/calendar labels;
  protect user content, retain English fallbacks and test catalogs/browser UI.
- Local server: Quietly handle broken pipes and reset/aborted client connections,
  including disconnects while reporting CGI errors; add regression coverage.
- Login/register: Replace password visibility text with Font Awesome eye icons
  matching WeKan, keeping independent toggles and descriptive tooltips.
- Login/register: Place independent visibility buttons to the right of both
  password inputs and match their white backgrounds and input styling.
- Layout: Match the current WeKan component ordering with native Gambas header,
  navigation, central views, sidebars and card/settings panels; add isolated
  Chromium desktop/mobile tests and correct floating-panel focus positioning.
- Local server: Fall back to a free port when 8080 is occupied, retain explicit
  port requests and verify binding/serving behavior with isolated socket tests.
- Login/register UI: Add password visibility controls, repeated-password validation
  and specific registration errors, with source/archive HTTP regression tests.
- Password policy: Accept short passwords by default and enforce a persisted
  minimum only when Admin Panel / Password Length enables it, with regression tests.
- Accounts: Register the first user as Admin and later users as Normal; remove
  seeded accounts, enforce permissions, hash passwords and test concurrent signups.
- Kanban: Add persistent boards/cards, archives, activities, profile/admin controls
  and embedded list, swimlane, table, calendar, milestone and chart views with tests.
- Build/release: Add the build/test/package menu, Flatpak Gambas copy helper,
  local CGI runtime, isolated HTTP tests and incremental all/missing release CI.
- Packaging: Add eight Linux CPU targets, WSL/Docker launchers and source archives
  with checksums; verify local ARM64 packaging and document unverified targets.
- Documentation: Add project-only instruction files, README build/release guidance
  and TODO tracking; record verified work separately from remaining feature parity.

